name metatex
category Package
revision 15878
shortdesc Incorporate Metafont pictures in TeX source
longdesc METATeX is a set of plain TeX and Metafont macros that you can
longdesc use to define both the text and the figures in a single source
longdesc file. Because METATeX sets up two way communication, from TeX
longdesc to Metafont and back from Metafont to TeX, drawing dimensions
longdesc can be controlled by TeX and labels can be located by Metafont.
longdesc Only standard features of TeX and Metafont are used, but two
longdesc runs of TeX and one of Metafont are needed.
